WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.892
"The Side Effects of the Hormones in Milk"

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.360
We've known for decades
that women who eat meat

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.760
have higher levels of estrogen
in their blood.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.320
Compared to nonvegetarians,
vegetarian women were found

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.160
to have 45 percent lower levels

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.320
of the most potent
human estrogen.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.320
This may help explain
the lower incidence

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.200
of breast cancer

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.200
among those eating
more plant-based.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.200
Even semi-vegetarians
who eat less meat

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.240
than omnivorous women

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.280
may have significantly lower
estrogen levels.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.320
Why?

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.880
Perhaps because
vegetarian women excrete

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.480
two to three times
more estrogens in their feces

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.720
than do
their meat-eating counterparts.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.640
And why is that?

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.840
Because the average
fecal output of vegetarians

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.520
can be twice as high.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.280
Look at those heavyweight Vs

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.840
compared to
the featherweight Os.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.480
The thought is that
because vegetarians eat

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.160
the amount of fiber
closer to that

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.240
which is natural
for our species,

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.840
those relying more on plants

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.440
have an increased fecal output,

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.600
which helps pull
excess estrogen

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.200
out of the system.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.480
It may also have
something to do

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:07.520
with the hormones present
in animal products.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.680
For example, the higher average
blood concentrations

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:10.960
of estrogen

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.280
associated
with high dairy consumption

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.400
would be consistent with milk
as a major source of estrogens

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.320
in the human diet.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.800
The reason we're concerned is
that the increased consumption

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.680
of animal-derived foods
may have adverse effects

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.360
on the development
of hormone-dependent cancers.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.800
Among dietary risk factors,

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.880
these investigators
were most concerned

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.560
about milk and dairy products,

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.280
because the milk we drink today

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.680
is produced by pregnant cows
with markedly elevated levels

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.480
of both estrogen
and progesterone.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.480
The genetic manipulation
of dairy cows

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.080
enables them to lactate

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.680
throughout almost
their entire pregnancies,

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.200
which is why
commercial cow's milk

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.800
contains large amounts
of estrogens

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.720
and progesterone these days.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.040
That may be why milk-drinkers

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.720
have five times the rates
of having twins

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.000
compared to vegans.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.600
That's how much of an effect
dairy may have on our hormones.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.240
But we don't really know how
much the hormones in dairy

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.960
affects our hormones
until we put it to the test.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.560
Researchers looked to see
what happens

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.960
when men
and prepubescent children,

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.600
who both would normally have
low estrogen levels,

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.360
chug a quart (950 ml)
of cow's milk

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.960
in under ten minutes.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.760
This is what happened
to the men.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.440
Within an hour
of drinking the milk,

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.199
their levels of the estrogen
estrone went up (and progesterone),

00:02:31.199 --> 00:02:36.049
and testosterone significantly
dropped within 60 minutes.

00:02:36.049 --> 00:02:37.280
It's funny, there are men

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.960
who don't want
to drink soy milk

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.720
because of the phytoestrogens,

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.320
even though soy phytoestrogens

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.600
normally does not have
feminizing effects on men,

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.640
yet they're perfectly willing
to drink cow's milk,

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:52.560
which has actual
estrogen estrogens in it!

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.880
In children, researchers saw
the same thing.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.120
The level of estrogens
flowing through their body

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.480
within an hour of drinking milk
more than tripled:

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.920
estrone, the potent estrogen
estradiol,

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.240
the pregnancy estrogen estriol,

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.320
and a progesterone metabolite.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:10.400
And half the kids
couldn't even finish

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.320
the whole quart (950 ml)
of milk.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.240
There's also another
sex steroid hormone

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:15.360
present in cow's milk

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.120
called 5alpha-P
(5alpha-pregnenedione)

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.560
which is a direct precursor
to a type of testosterone

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.040
that may not only drive acne

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.320
but also promote
prostate cancer.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.960
Now, we'd like to see
controlled clinical studies,

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.760
but the problem is
there is no control.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:37.440
Dairy without the offending
estrogens does not exist.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.800
Even organic milk from cows
who aren't injected

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.600
with extra hormones
has growth hormones in it,

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:47.040
because biologically,
that's the whole point of milk,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.920
to put a couple of hundred
pounds on a baby calf.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.240
The problem with humans
drinking cow hormones

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.880
is that there's
no natural feedback loop.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.240
For our own hormones,

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:57.760
if we have too much estrogen
or something,

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.720
our brain dampens it down.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.360
But our own protective
feedback system is bypassed

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.960
when our system is invaded

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.520
by these dihydrotestosterone
precursors

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.200
in dairy products.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.720
See, the human
endocrine system,

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.240
our hormonal system,

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.320
didn't evolve
under the influence

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.960
of ingested dairy
and other external hormones

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.640
and growth factors,
and we're just not equipped

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:21.840
to cope with such
a quote-unquote "sneak attack."

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.600
In summary, evidence suggests

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:26.240
that consumption
of dairy-sourced hormones,

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.000
which aren't subject to any
innate feedback inhibition,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.320
may be the source
of the steroid sex hormones

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:35.840
that drive acne
and at least prostate cancer.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.800
This is perhaps the most
promising unifying hypothesis—

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.160
or theory—

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:42.480
to explain the cause
of diverse conditions

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:48.686
that blemish, scar, shorten,
or take the lives of millions.

